course: dictionary
lesson: 7734
title: Simple machines: the pulley
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pulley is a simple machine: a wheel with a groove around its edge, and a rope or chain runs over it. Pulling the rope down can lift a heavy load up, which is much easier than lifting it straight up.
explain: «One fixed pulley changes the direction of the force, so you can pull down to lift up.» The force you push or pull with is not made smaller by one pulley. It is only turned to point the other way.
explain: «Thread a rope through several pulleys and the load hangs on many lengths of rope that share its weight.» Because the weight is shared, you pull with less force, but you must pull much more rope.
fact: A pulley is one of the simple machines, with the lever, the wheel and axle, and the ramp.
fact: A pulley is a wheel with a groove that a rope or chain runs over.
fact: Several pulleys share the load, so you pull with less force but must pull much more rope.
fact: Flagpoles, cranes and wells use pulleys to lift things.
fact: A crane uses pulleys with a heavy counterweight that balances the load like a seesaw.
exercise: What is a pulley? | A kind of lever only | *A simple machine: a wheel with a groove for a rope or chain | A type of cloud | A box with a lid
exercise: «One fixed pulley changes the direction of the force.» What does this let you do? | Pull up to lift up | Pull sideways only | Lift without any rope | *Pull down to lift up
exercise: «Thread a rope through several pulleys.» What do several pulleys do? | Make the load heavier | Stop the rope from moving | *Let you pull with less force but must pull more rope | Change the rope into a chain
test: Which of these is a simple machine? | The well | *The ramp | The flagpole | The crane
test: Why does a crane have a heavy counterweight? | To make it louder | To make it taller | *To balance the load like a seesaw | To hold the rope still
exam: A builder uses several pulleys to lift a load. Why does she pull with less force but must pull more rope? | *Because the load's weight is shared by many lengths of rope | Because pulleys make the load lighter in weight | Because the rope gets longer when it is pulled | Because the wheels turn backwards
